    "summary": "Ulu with metal blade and stem, and carved wooden handle. Handle rectangular with upper corners rounded, underside from stem out to corners slightly concave on both sides; highly polished, probably painted with warm red-brown; several cracks (not deep). Stem inserted into handle and probably glued. Blade is set in stem and fastened with metal plug and probably glued; blade rounded on lower side, sharpened from one side, upper sides forming angle of ca 135 degrees, slightly concave, and rounded near the stem; one corner of blade &quot;higher&quot; than the other.",
